From 34442a6f1a6fc1eea66512198235817c7a29a3f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hadron <dev@hadron.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:27:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: Use per-thread W^X JIT code buffers on macOS.

Apple silicon macOS refuses RWX mappings, so Wine maps PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE
memory writable and flips 16K host pages to executable on an execute fault and
back on a write fault. FEX alternates writing and running code on the same
pages whenever it compiles, loads from the disk cache or links blocks, so
every such write cost two faults and two mprotect() calls.

Ask Wine for MAP_JIT-backed code buffers instead
(MEM_EXTENDED_PARAMETER_WINE_UNIX_JIT) when the unixlib reports that
pthread_jit_write_protect_np() is supported, and switch the calling thread
to write mode around every write to a CodeBuffer: copying compiled or
disk-cached code in, block linking, block delinking (batched per
invalidation), unaligned-atomic backpatching and the code cache's
relocation passes. The toggle is a unix call. Scopes don't nest, as TLS
isn't usable in FEX's Windows modules. Elsewhere ScopedJITWrite is a no-op
and VirtualAllocJIT allocates RWX memory as before.
